Publish NSScreenNumber, without which no display id maps back to a screen.

Qt asks CoreGraphics for the online displays, gets one with id 1, and then looks for the NSScreen
whose deviceDescription NSScreenNumber matches it. Our deviceDescription had five keys and that
was not one of them, so the search found nothing and Qt kept

    QCocoaScreen(..., QRect(0,684 0x0), dpr=0, displayId=1) as new primary screen

a screen with NO SIZE and a device pixel ratio of ZERO. Every window it then made was 1x1.

INVISIBLE TO ANYTHING THAT ONLY ASKS APPKIT, which is why five roster applications never noticed:
they take their screen from NSScreen directly and never go round by a display id. The Wayland
backend also never set the id, so it was 0, while the X11 backend beside it does set index plus 1
(X11Display.m). CGGetOnlineDisplayList and CGDisplayBounds both number from 1 by index, so 1 is
the value that agrees with them.

Spelled as the literal @"NSScreenNumber" because the constant is not declared in these headers.

MEASURED AFTER, same run shape:
    QCocoaScreen(..., QRect(0,0 1256x684), dpr=1, displayId=1,
      < <NSScreen: 0x...> - frame {{0, 0}, {1256, 684}}, visible {{0, 0}, {1256, 684}} >)

NOT THE WHOLE OF #227. The four windows Qt makes during QApplication init are still 1x1 and the
application still exits without showing its own window. This removes a defect that was certainly
wrong and would mislead any toolkit doing the same lookup; what CMake does next is still open.

--- a/AppKit/NSScreen.m
+++ b/AppKit/NSScreen.m
@@ -161,7 +161,15 @@
 - (NSDictionary<NSDeviceDescriptionKey, id> *) deviceDescription {
     CGFloat dpi = 72.0 * [self backingScaleFactor];
 
+    /*
+     * NSScreenNumber IS HOW A CALLER GETS FROM A CGDirectDisplayID BACK TO A SCREEN, and leaving it
+     * out is invisible to anything that only ever asks AppKit. Qt asks CoreGraphics for the online
+     * displays, then looks for the NSScreen whose NSScreenNumber matches; with the key absent that
+     * search finds nothing, so it kept a screen of QRect(0,684 0x0) with dpr=0 and built every
+     * window 1x1 on it. Spelled literally because the constant is not declared in these headers.
+     */
     return @{
+        @"NSScreenNumber" : [NSNumber numberWithUnsignedInt: _directDisplayID],
         NSDeviceResolution : [NSValue valueWithSize: NSMakeSize(dpi, dpi)],
         NSDeviceSize : [NSValue valueWithSize: _frame.size],
         NSDeviceIsScreen : @"YES",
